    "text": "Let the foci of a hyperbola $H$ coincide with the foci of the ellipse $E: \\frac{(x-1)^2}{100}+\\frac{(y-1)^2}{75}=1$ and the eccentricity of the hyperbola $H$ be the reciprocal of the eccentricity of the ellipse $E$. If the length of the transverse axis of $H$ is $\\alpha$ and the length of its conjugate axis is $\\beta$, then $3 \\alpha^2+2 \\beta^2$ is equal to"
